161
00:11:34.792 --> 00:11:41.811
(narrator) Four questions try the idea on new cases: a sort algorithm, prices in cents, a payment method's return type, and a database swap.

162
00:11:42.427 --> 00:11:46.027
♪ Pop quiz! Y2K: what got copied everywhere? ♪

163
00:11:46.027 --> 00:11:47.467
♪ (crowd) The two-digit year! ♪

164
00:11:47.467 --> 00:11:50.567
♪ Your sort is quicksort. Secret, or contract? ♪

165
00:11:50.567 --> 00:11:53.147
♪ (crowd) Secret! They just want it sorted! ♪

166
00:11:53.147 --> 00:11:56.147
♪ Prices come back in cents. Secret, or contract? ♪

167
00:11:56.147 --> 00:11:59.107
♪ (crowd) Contract! Callers need to know! ♪

168
00:11:59.107 --> 00:12:02.247
♪ Private field, but pay() returns a PayPal Charge. Hidden? ♪

169
00:12:02.247 --> 00:12:04.727
